### 9. Decisions I made

1. **Coalescing `signal_events` across `earlyWaveCheck_` and `edDrainQueue_` within `poll()`**: In [Main.gs](file:///Users/lhammonds/Desktop/burson-triage-agent/apps-script-chat-bot/Main.gs#L575-L593), `ctx._ewBqDeferEvents = true` defers flushing `earlyWaveCheck_`'s `signal_events` (`queued`, `filtered_fast_triage`, `held_repeat`) so `edDrainQueue_` merges them with its own `signal_events` (`dropped_stale`, `reviewed`, `carded`, `update_posted`) and sends a single `bqInsertAll_` request to `early_wave.signal_events` per run.
2. **PII & tracking-parameter stripping on `early_wave` rows**: In [ewBqUrl_](file:///Users/lhammonds/Desktop/burson-triage-agent/apps-script-chat-bot/FastTriage.gs#L507-L514) and [ewBqAccountKey_](file:///Users/lhammonds/Desktop/burson-triage-agent/apps-script-chat-bot/FastTriage.gs#L517-L522), post URLs are canonicalized (`ewsCanonUrl_`, stripping `utm_*` and other tracking parameters) and raw author handles/IDs are hashed (`acct_${ewsFnv_}`) before writing `story_posts` and `signals.sample_posts`, guaranteeing zero raw handles, emails, or tracking tokens ever enter `brand-social-central-data.early_wave`.
3. **Strict isolation from `slrr.slrr_alerts`**: In [bqInsertAll_](file:///Users/lhammonds/Desktop/burson-triage-agent/apps-script-chat-bot/BigQuery.gs#L430-L433), `BQ_WRITEBACK_EVER_PROP_` is skipped whenever the target dataset is `early_wave`, so turning Row 46 ON never affects Row 16 (`Write back to SLRR BigQuery`) or `slrr.slrr_alerts`.

